There should be an altar and prayer spoiler around somewhere. Basically,
if you sacrifice and get "a hopeful feeling" you're not ready to pray
yet; if you see four-leaf clovers your luck has gone up; if you have a
feeling of reconciliation you can now pray safely; if nothing happens,
it's OK to pray and if you've been sacrificing for some time, your luck
is at maximum. If you now keep sacrificing, your god may give you a
cool thing.

It's usually a good idea not to pray immediately just because you can;
save it for when you need something. Try dropping plain (uncursed)
water or unholy water on the altar and then praying.
 
>> I never knew rings made you more hungry!
> I didn't either. Is that for sure?

Chargeable rings that aren't +0 (so, probably, negatively enchanted ones
as well) and all non-chargeable rings make you more hungry.
Regeneration and hunger (duh) make you much more hungry. Even the ring
of slow digestion makes you more hungry, but it negates all other
normal hunger effects so the net effect is that you get hungry much
more slowly.
 
